<Rive version="1" kind="fragment">
    <!-- arch-draw - the fuime mark builds itself.

         Two copies of the same geometry, because one shape cannot both trim a
         stroke and clip a fill: a ClippingShape masks the whole shape, stroke
         included. So "Outline" carries the stroke that draws on, "Solid"
         carries the fill that floods up behind it, and the two are keyed to
         overlap in the middle of the timeline.

         The flood direction is not arbitrary. The site's loader already fills
         the arch from the bottom (site/index.html), and an asset that fills it
         the other way reads as a different brand.

         The vertices are generated - tools/svg2rml.py against
         site/img/favicon.svg. Regenerate rather than hand-edit them. -->

    <Artboard defaultStateMachineId="0:7" styleId="0:5" width="600" height="600" name="Arch" id="0:2">
        <LayoutComponentStyle name="Artboard Style" id="0:5"/>

        <!-- The assembly, so one keyed scale settles the whole mark. -->
        <Node x="300" y="300" name="Mark" id="0:10">

            <!-- Declared first, so it draws in front of the fill it outlines. -->
            <Shape x="-300" y="-300" name="Outline" id="0:14">
